libdtfl NEWS -- user-visible changes, newest first.

Version 0.1.0 (unreleased)

	First development release.

	A C11 port of timely dataflow (pinned at timely-v0.31.0),
	differential dataflow (differential-dataflow-v0.25.1), and the
	timely diagnostics tools.  Functionally complete: the timely
	runtime and all operators across five execution modes (single
	thread, threads, processes, simulated, and a TCP cluster);
	differential collections, traces, and shared arrangements; join,
	reduce, iterate, count, threshold, and distinct; the graph
	algorithms and the dogsdogsdogs worst-case-optimal joins; the
	diagnostics WebSocket server with the dtfl-diag program; and the
	DDIR dataflow compiler with the dtfl-ddir and dtfl-server tools.

	Thread-safe, with allocation, panic, logging, and thread hooks for
	embedding (for example in PostgreSQL).  A Texinfo manual and 73 man
	pages, both gate-checked.  Validated on Linux x86_64 (gcc), FreeBSD
	(clang), and Linux riscv64 (gcc).

	Known limitation in this release, tracked in
	dev/P15-measurements.md: performance behind the Rust originals,
	about 8 times slower on the arrange benchmark and about 29 times
	slower on count throughput after a first optimisation pass, the
	structural cost of the fidelity-first record and container
	decisions.  Closing it to the 1.5x goal is the main item before a
	1.0 release.
